 **Reason:** Classic Tetris scoring rewards multi-line clears exponentially, motivating strategic play. Using `pygame.font.Font(None, 36)` picks the default font at a readable size without requiring external assets.
 
 **Consequences:** The board is rebuilt each time lines are cleared (filtering full rows, padding with empties). For a 10×20 board this is negligible. Score persistence across line clears is straightforward since `self.score` is an integer attribute.
 
+### ADR-008: Game over detection and restart for Milestone 8
+
+**Decision:** After `spawn_piece`, check if the new piece can be placed using `_can_place`. If not, set `self.game_over = True`. While game over, stop processing movement/rotation/gravity inputs. Pressing R calls `_restart()` to reset board, score, and spawn a new piece. "GAME OVER" text is rendered centered on screen with a "Press R to restart" hint below.
+
+**Reason:** Game over in Tetris occurs when a newly spawned piece immediately collides with placed blocks — the stack has reached the top. Detecting this at spawn time is simpler than checking after every lock. Restart via R key gives the player control over when to retry, avoiding automatic restart that could feel jarring.
+
+**Consequences:** The game over state halts all game logic but keeps the window open (doesn't quit). This preserves the rendered board so the player can see how they lost. The `_restart()` method resets all mutable state to initial values, making it a clean reset without reinitializing pygame.
+
